</style>
<h2>Asobi 0.2 (build 291)</h2>
<p><b>Full drawing-tool parity on the web, and links a tenth the length.</b></p>
<ul>
<li>The web toolbar now matches the app: pointer (default — and it moves marks by dragging, just like the app), pen, arrow, box, ellipse, text with wrapping boxes, eraser, fill with its own opacity, and stroke width. Esc returns to the pointer; native seats see the web pointer as a presence cursor.</li>
<li>Fixed: moving a mark in the app never told anyone — the new position now reaches every peer, native and web.</li>
<li>Review links are ~63 characters (was ~400): the public invite fields live behind a short code and the encryption key still travels only in the link fragment, never to any server.</li>
<li>Web reviewers can add session-wide notes (the app's Global Comments) from the notes panel.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
